 knight on e5 and threatening …Bxb2+, winning the queen and a rook. Then 29…Qc7 uncovers an attack on the rook on b2, and 30…Qxb8 takes the rook on b8. Black is a pawn down: Black holds the balance (+0.06). This is White's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 27…Bf8, is clearly weaker (+0.87 against 0.00). White answers 28.f3, preparing f4 and Nf3. That would leave Black a little worse."}]},{"ply":57,"name":"29.Rc3","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"29.Rc3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Protects the rook on b2, which was hanging.","The next best move, 29.Rc2, would drop White's winning chances from 50% to 8% (−6.71).","29.Rc3 stops …Bxb2+.","Black was threatening …Bxb2+, winning the queen and a rook. Rc3 takes care of it.","The rook on c3 can be taken by the bishop on e5.","Black answers 29…Qa7, winning the exchange."]},{"ply":65,"name":"33.c7","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"33.c7! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Pushes the passed pawn to c7, close to promotion.","Takes b8 away from the Black queen on b5.","The next best move, 33.e4, would drop White's winning chances from 40% to 7% (−7.10).","33.c7 threatens c8=Q+, promoting to a queen.","It threatens c8=Q+, promoting to a queen, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","Black answers 33…Qc6, winning a pawn."]},{"ply":67,"name":"34.Kb2","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"34.Kb2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The next best move, 34.c8=R+, would drop White's winning chances from 44% to 17% (−4.32).","34.Kb2 stops …Bxc3+.","Black was threatening …Bxc3+, winning a rook. Kb2 takes care of it.","The engine's plan continues with Kc2 and Qf6: this move is the first step.","Black answers 34…Qxc7, winning the exchange.","After 34…Qxc7 35.Kc2 Bxc3 36.Qxc3 Qb8 37.Qf6, White is a piece down (−0.33)."]},{"ply":68,"name":"34…Qxc7","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"34…Qxc7! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the pawn on c7.","The next best move, 34…Kh7, would drop Black's winning chances from 53% to 14% (+4.97).","34…Qxc7 wins a pawn and threatens …Qc4, winning the exchange, picking it up with 36…Bxc3.","Takes the c7 pawn and wins a pawn once the captures settle.","It threatens …Qc4, winning the exchange, picking it up with 36…Bxc3, so White has to spend the next move on it.","White answers 35.Qb4."]},{"ply":87,"name":"44.Qe5","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"44.Qe5 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 50% to 19%.","points":["Black answers 44…Qb1: the queen joins the attack: it now hits 5 squares around the White king.","After Qb1, Black wins 1 point of material within 4 moves.","Better was 44.Kc3 (0.00)."],"better":"44.Kc3 wins a pawn, picking it up with 45.Qxe5. After 44…e5 45.Qxe5 Qh3 46.Kb4 Qxh4 47.Qxd5 Kg8, White comes out a pawn up (0.00)."},{"ply":88,"name":"44…Qb1","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"44…Qb1! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The queen joins the attack: it now hits 5 squares around the White king.","Attacks the a2 pawn, which is undefended.","The next best move, 44…d4, would drop Black's winning chances from 81% to 51% (−0.12).","44…Qb1 wins a pawn, picking it up with 45…Qxa2+.","Sets up a sequence and wins a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 45…Qxa2+.","White answers 45.Qf6, attacking the f7 pawn, which is undefended."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Gambit Declined","eco":"D53","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 9…g6: 18 moves in all, 9 by White and 9 by Black.","Theory runs out after 9…g6: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}